# Forces local-only mode regardless of a developer's .env.
#
# Every screenshot gate (material, definition-of-done, motion, console,
# acceptance, commit-flow) assumes the app is in local mode: they score against
# seeded data and never sign in. Once a real .env exists, `npm run dev` boots
# backed and every one of those routes redirects to /signin — the gates go red
# for a reason that has nothing to do with the change under test.
#
# Vite applies .env.[mode] after .env, so blank values here win. Committed on
# purpose: this is gate configuration, not a secret.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
